    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">VPSDime is a strong choice for developers who know exactly what they need from a server and want the most RAM per dollar without dealing with teaser pricing. The 12 GB entry plan at $6/mo is genuinely unusual in the budget VPS space — you'd pay $20-40 for equivalent RAM at DigitalOcean or Vultr. The trade-off is a stripped-down experience: no managed support, no automated backups, a minimal client area. If you're comfortable setting up your own monitoring and backup scripts, VPSDime delivers exceptional hardware value. For beginners who need hand-holding or one-click app installs, a provider like ScalaHosting or KnownHost would be a better fit.</p>
